1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,780
The air can't keep
up with the ground.

2
00:00:05,258 --> 00:00:07,023
It is pulled along
only by friction,

3
00:00:07,023 --> 00:00:09,078
so for the first hours
it is left behind.

4
00:00:09,580 --> 00:00:11,030
The ground
moves through it

5
00:00:11,030 --> 00:00:13,675
at about 1,040 miles
an hour.

6
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:17,470
The strongest
gust ever measured

7
00:00:17,470 --> 00:00:20,220
was about 250 miles
an hour.

8
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:24,010
This wind would be 4×
faster,

9
00:00:24,010 --> 00:00:26,855
blowing from the east,
because

10
00:00:26,855 --> 00:00:29,255
the ground is running
ahead of the air.

11
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:31,295
Winds like that would
strip the surface,

12
00:00:31,295 --> 00:00:33,055
and they'd only
be the beginning.

13
00:00:34,532 --> 00:00:36,737
If you're enjoying this,
tap like and follow.

14
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:40,525
And then the oceans
start to move.
